<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed weaker at 2.24 pct from parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed weaker at 2.24 pct from parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.1470 to the dollar, up from 3.1515 on Tuesday and at 1.8650 to the mark, down from 1.8575, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 2.24 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, weaker than Tuesday's 2.40 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
